{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for sales-design draft5 at exact4c082db8b9dde79dcd2c6f97aca7426d92c93052 / treef7112adafaf004cf88e6057366e8d1d8643e2576, primaryfe6e7ef1, notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md. Full607-line primary read, including the new product-positioning section. F1 and F4 of19d0bbfd are resolved. F2, F3 and F5 are substantially improved but still need the concrete corrections below.\n\nF1 resolved: separate static-grant supply actions, domain and assigned-expert signer guards, shared explicit bid.review, per-kind approvals, and human-only asking now fit existing declared grant forms. Routing is explicitly an offer, not authority.\n\nF4 resolved: retirement uses a notice and index rewrite as separate file publications, each with its own outcome; repository deletion is deferred. This fits today's write-only publish-file.\n\nF2 high — Do not implement the required-approval fix by opening three local items in one declared act (5.2 lines328ff and5.3 line396). The note now says intake creates the bid plus both requested approval items. A declared open act opens its one primary item; also selects existing items, and EffectForm has no extra local open. The judge passes only act.on to derive's single opening (contract/src/definition.ts ActType, AlsoRule and EffectForm; derive/src/judge.ts:379; derive/src/effects.ts:312). Choose an explicit supported sequence: for example, open the bid, separately open the uniquely guarded price and terms approvals once their requirements exist, and retain the strong assembly presence/current-revision guards; or keep the two approvals as slots on the bid. A bounded message sequence with one opening per handler is another existing-form option if the note states that protocol and blocks assembly until it completes. Do not imply a multi-open effect or automatic atomic initialization that the declared form lacks.\n\nThe all-row/current-approval/immutable-assembly prose and revised forty-row refusal/completion witness correctly address the earlier completeness problem. Preserve them. Also state which imports are required/current: 'every confirmed import' must not allow assembly to ignore a required read/mapped/unconfirmed import merely because it has not been confirmed yet. The active-import policy in F5 can make this simple.\n\nF3 high — Specify authority and authenticated evidence for record-publication, and compare the whole expected publication identity (5.2/5.3 and6.2/6.3). Pending/unknown/refused/superseded states and no blind resend are now correct. But record-publication is absent from both grant tables, and its act description confirms when the digest matches without stating the native guard or authenticated readback mechanism. A signed act with a user-supplied 'receipt' is that signer's report; a matching content digest alone is not the destination's confirmation. Two different paths, send ordinals or incarnations can publish identical text and share the digest.\n\nName the fixed action/authorized recorder and an existing authenticated destination fact or checked readback path. Require matching the expected full sending scope/incarnation, source fact, ordinal, path and content digest, plus a confirmed publication outcome; refused, superseded, missing and unknown results cannot set confirmed. If the first version records a member's report of an external receipt check instead of validating that outcome natively, say that and preserve its attribution instead of claiming independent destination-confirmed state. The reusable-library publication/readback mechanism may be used, but its actual trust boundary must be named. No new general operation framework is required.\n\nF5 medium — Bound the actual complete query source, not each import independently, and retain byte limits (5.2 and5.4 lines290ff,448ff). A100-row-per-import bound still admits two60-row imports in the same bid, or a replacement import while the earlier requirements remain in queried states. The carousel's many source then contains120 rows and refuses before for can route it. The note explicitly permits a changed spreadsheet as a new import and checks every confirmed import, so this is a live path, not a hypothetical feature. State a finite aggregate bound across the active requirement source and an old-import/requirement disposition. A single active import per bid, with an explicit replacement protocol, is a sufficient small first version if that is the intended choice. Block incomplete required imports at assembly as noted in F2.\n\nAlso choose conservative row/text/payload bounds rather than promising100 arbitrary-size drafts/answers: source/result payload is capped at256KiB and list/value limits still apply. Require oversized input/expansion to refuse before misleading partial work, or choose a smaller safe first-version bound and defer larger requests. The101-row refusal witness is useful but does not exercise aggregate imports or oversized rows. This requests a bounded design contract, not larger limits or generic paging.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: the three packages, supplied-answer/team-review split, buyer outside the first bid room, multiple owned scopes credited to M2a and M2b, and integrations deferred behind plan033 are coherent. Explicit item-opening steps and a bounded active-import set keep the design within existing forms. Publication needs a named confirmation path as well as correct lifecycle labels. Hosted agent teams remain proposed, not landed execution for these sales flows.\n\nSecurity conclusion: F1 correctly makes domain and assigned-party decisions native. Keep local approval/sealing distinct from destination evidence and from manually reported channel actions. Exact receipt cause matching and recorder authority are necessary to prevent the newly added confirmation act from accepting the wrong publication or an unverified report. Links and digests remain references, not private source-file custody.\n\nSimplification conclusion: keep F1's static acts and F4's existing writes. Separate ordinary approval-opening steps (or bid slots), one bounded active import policy and one explicit receipt trust boundary solve the remaining issues without a multi-open extension, new integration framework or higher projection bounds. The added 'Why not just an agent' section explains shared signed decisions and replaceable agents; it is a design argument, not evidence that these unimplemented packages or archival/hosted workflows already run.\n\nValidation: entire draft5 read in full after an initial tool-output truncation was corrected by a standalone full read; authored diff reviewed against1469 and Main2127. Only this Markdown path changes; all10 local links/fragments resolve; whitespace clean. SHA256b0ffb5b3740fdc04aca9a88e6ce1e3a46d77c11987786b2b41eb2da456fa55b7. Native prepare binds7f569087/28988cd9/reportfe6 at this exact head. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-sales-design-jne3y8sq retains primary/validation. Existing landed contract/judge/projection/publication source checks reused; no source/test edits, package install, test/gate rerun, provider/publication/deployment action.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fe6e7ef19a22e730c8ea4431277ebe16c32471ae","binding":"assigned","head":"4c082db8b9dde79dcd2c6f97aca7426d92c93052","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d6f1e3df21b5fbc3d0b5bcc72d3a4b1034b24482\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28988cd98dfb9eddaadb8934b253cc352c17814f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d6f1e3df21b5fbc3d0b5bcc72d3a4b1034b24482","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}